1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:09,656
Deep dive: library templates. Tune a cabinet once, keep it in the library, and every job after that starts from your shop’s standard.

2
00:00:09,656 --> 00:00:38,697
Templates: the built-in presets, then this shop’s own US sizes. The Novak kitchen was built from these.

3
00:00:38,697 --> 00:00:46,176
The shop decides every 24" base gets two shelves from now on. Edit the template itself.

4
00:00:46,176 --> 00:00:56,390
The banner says the key rule: existing jobs keep their own copy. A job you have already priced or cut never changes behind your back.

5
00:00:56,390 --> 00:01:10,590
It is the same editor as a job cabinet. Shelves: 1 to 2.

6
00:01:10,590 --> 00:01:16,825
New cabinets from this template get two shelves. For jobs already drawn, it is your call: Update existing jobs…

7
00:01:16,825 --> 00:01:30,101
It lists the cabinets copied from this template: in J2061, the Novak kitchen, B1 and B5. Not cut yet, so update them.

8
00:01:30,101 --> 00:01:52,480
Back in the job, B1 now has two shelves. Updating replaces the construction; the cabinet stays where it is in the room.

9
00:01:52,480 --> 00:02:05,348
The other way round: tune a cabinet in a job, then save it. This 3-drawer base gets 15 in slides, for a run with plumbing behind it.

10
00:02:05,348 --> 00:02:15,979
Save as template. It saves the parameters only: one-off edge overrides stay with this job’s cabinet, so a template stays clean.

11
00:02:15,979 --> 00:02:31,282
Name it for what makes it different, and say when to use it. The next person to pick it will know.

12
00:02:31,282 --> 00:02:43,777
It is in the library now, with your description, next to the others.

13
00:02:43,777 --> 00:02:52,670
Export bundle saves templates, materials, edgebands and hardware as one file. Import bundle on the office PC and both use the same standards.

14
00:02:52,670 --> 00:03:20,401
Reuse: a new job for a wet bar, J2070. Add cabinet, and the new template is in the list.

15
00:03:20,401 --> 00:03:36,579
Open it: 15 in slides already set. No re-entering, and no chance of forgetting the one setting that matters on this job.

16
00:03:36,579 --> 00:03:41,872
So: edit a template to change the standard, update old jobs only when you choose, and save good cabinets back to the library.
